<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sonderbund War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sonderbund">Sonderbund</a> War was a brief civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a> in November 1847, in which the federal army under General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillaume-henri-dufour">Guillaume-Henri Dufour</a> defeated the Sonderbund, a league of seven Catholic cantons, in under a month and with roughly a hundred dead. It was the last armed conflict on Swiss soil, and its outcome cleared the way for the federal constitution of 1848 and the modern Swiss federal state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sonderbund-war.jpg" alt="Sonderbund War" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Translation by User:Sandstein, original by Marco Zanoli (Sidonius) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sonderbund_War_Map_English.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
